    "summary": "Knife and sheath, the knife with single-edged iron blade and wood handle, the sheath of carved reindeer bone with leather grip. The sheath formed of two pieces of bone hollowed and incised with interlocking circles, the two pieces held together by two iron pegs at the curved end and by the f grip at the other. The grip formed of one piece of leather, stamped with geometric patterns, and sewn together forming an integral loop through which a leather attachment thong is threaded.\r\n     The knife handle and the sheath marked in ink Y101",
